{"title":"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number such that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/6514e5c2f1b5f00055a46e13a0f7bc3a8b3ed885.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot(\\sin{x}+\\sin{(2x)}) = \\sin{(3x)}\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"18\" />\nhas more than one solution in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9dbd13d255bcea5d73d3fb36e7f92ebc9d314db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, \\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />. The set of all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that can be written\nin the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/753fb68fe13dda58b70a340f28da137c751bdbf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p,q) \\cup (q,r),\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec2b6f850a38c18bff9b2d860b248982102966e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are real numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e7ecfd53dc0e98daa12539cd01007bc21533b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &lt; q&lt; r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08ff3681d6992f69ee41e21c7237c89f970ac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d43851e3a8fbb7ad694e276808482345eb027a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } {-}4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } {-}1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"383\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a5b1fb3aa6b19bbef2964c332a42de9855fd799.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot(\\sin{x}+\\sin{(2x)})=\\sin{(3x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Using the sine double angle formula combine with the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa778bf978dda1a3ddfa849122dd75336d117067.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(3x)} = \\sin{x}\\cdot(4\\cos^2{x}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"237\" height=\"21\" />, which can be derived using sine angle addition with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b9ff9ae3c91102bcee5e2426fe9702a69b1011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(2x + x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e379cc785115c8b79d1899b7bc57e218f2ef0932.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot(\\sin{x}+2\\sin{x}\\cos{x})=\\sin{x}\\cdot(4\\cos^2{x}-1)\\]\" width=\"357\" height=\"20\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64656f53977b7d71e661ab661ef9ac0e97c256c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x} \\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> as it is on the open interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9dbd13d255bcea5d73d3fb36e7f92ebc9d314db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, \\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />, we can divide out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41470508df2ceb87f97c7e939589024bceb16e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> from both sides, leaving us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a712a8ab5fa9370a99cd9d581353ccd2ca48c440.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot(1+2\\cos{x})=4\\cos^2{x}-1\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />\nNow, distributing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and rearranging, we achieve the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311abaac7ad0642361a2b90158b48751bb6f4354.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4\\cos^2{x} - 2a\\cos{x} - (1+a) = 0\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"20\" /> which is a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cfae39cb378f17672726fb1de7705b94a6da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" />.\n</p><p>Applying the quadratic formula to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cfae39cb378f17672726fb1de7705b94a6da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a728e0aa90abca620fbe1fd5bca1bf9328fba5b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos{x} =\\frac{2a\\pm\\sqrt{4a^2+4(4)(1+a)}}{8}\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"41\" /> and expanding the terms under the radical, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6c28419e76045f056262025047e2d585b3fa10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos{x} =\\frac{2a\\pm\\sqrt{4a^2+16a+16}}{8}\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"40\" />\nFactoring, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eec13d402177894819e25e5a528465ec659baae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4a^2+16a+16 = (2a+4)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"21\" />, we can simplify our expression even further to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/0/2701df7aaeae25ad5b4ca77333c8fca618b3044d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos{x} =\\frac{a\\pm(a+2)}{4}\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now, solving for our two solutions,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e5fbdf2baef6adfb7afc2bad37264c14f25e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96699243fd5810906ec792f6c4fa32d62748a0ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = \\frac{a+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e5fbdf2baef6adfb7afc2bad37264c14f25e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> yields a solution that is valid for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, that being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45f2fd965805ffdf82d87289feebfe7a066b91ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />, we must now solve for the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/97439a3cb35d6366b2b48331bc36d5bb25cf1839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" /> yields a valid value.\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/87019fbc3cc63480a5ba09a7f5f849f631de7a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in (0, \\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37d044671dff71ee797e0c0b69fffa5e85453455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}\\in (-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920406c5b015e2cf0f34d360f0dbd34f4e2fb7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2}\\in (-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db6eb5b2af6d802bdd358693f1620d5dbaf21c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in(-3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>There is one more case we must consider inside this interval though, the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/62786145b090ff4897077ebea937cc54535b1e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />, as this would lead to a double root for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cfae39cb378f17672726fb1de7705b94a6da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" />, yielding only one valid solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Solving for this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66ce17754e2fee6f9e17faae5aee1c59462933e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ne -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, combining this fact with our solution interval, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420a07b9562ef0dd0bbf38bb005ac558e583b7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in(-3, -2) \\cup (-2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/3556324278fb89ba520dd02e3d8f119466a31583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3-2+1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } {-}4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>- DavidHovey\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can optimize from the step from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a712a8ab5fa9370a99cd9d581353ccd2ca48c440.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot(1+2\\cos{x})=4\\cos^2{x}-1\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" /> in solution 1 by writing\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/e/06e2f390f128d3363fe74a59898edbb233f0e2f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\frac{4\\cos^2{x}-1}{1+2\\cos{x}} = 2\\cos x - 1\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>and then get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf2c5eb2d792d0dd3a13d09efb12d79e9613463.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos x = \\frac{a+1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now, solving for our two solutions,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e5fbdf2baef6adfb7afc2bad37264c14f25e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96699243fd5810906ec792f6c4fa32d62748a0ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = \\frac{a+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e5fbdf2baef6adfb7afc2bad37264c14f25e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> yields a solution that is valid for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, that being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45f2fd965805ffdf82d87289feebfe7a066b91ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />, we must now solve for the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/97439a3cb35d6366b2b48331bc36d5bb25cf1839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" /> yields a valid value.\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/87019fbc3cc63480a5ba09a7f5f849f631de7a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in (0, \\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37d044671dff71ee797e0c0b69fffa5e85453455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}\\in (-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920406c5b015e2cf0f34d360f0dbd34f4e2fb7a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2}\\in (-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db6eb5b2af6d802bdd358693f1620d5dbaf21c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in(-3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>There is one more case we must consider inside this interval though, the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/62786145b090ff4897077ebea937cc54535b1e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+1}{2} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />, as this would lead to a double root for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cfae39cb378f17672726fb1de7705b94a6da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x}$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" />, yielding only one valid solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Solving for this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66ce17754e2fee6f9e17faae5aee1c59462933e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ne -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, combining this fact with our solution interval, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420a07b9562ef0dd0bbf38bb005ac558e583b7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in(-3, -2) \\cup (-2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/3556324278fb89ba520dd02e3d8f119466a31583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3-2+1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } {-}4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>- Dan\n</p><p>Remark: If you get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f75ca5a656b38e0a3ab566324d17c9c0abdaacc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\in (-3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />, then you can observe from the answer choices that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd17533ad95a4593f77c702ed1c730c264848d0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2, 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> or something greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then you can guess that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b00c96499972dcece6a927ae01957dc79c0be1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> can't be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the sum to product formula to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e494457fe877055e73395e3ad3d8bed4f77dd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a\\cdot\\sin{\\frac{3x}{2}}\\cos{\\frac{x}{2}}=\\sin{3x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"196\" height=\"38\" />. Use the double angle formula on the RHS to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9ae3c7d91e9f6c873d329a430b62d7d7c8f09fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot\\sin{\\frac{3x}{2}}\\cos{\\frac{x}{2}}=\\sin{\\frac{3x}{2}}\\cos{\\frac{3x}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"245\" height=\"38\" />. From here, it is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c0a0bc6cbf65c1a64b7c907716f335ed011177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"37\" /> is always a solution, and thus we divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b37b477a22360e3d81415de63fbd1e28353318e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\frac{3x}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea7482705923e3202b5786d40921d69629bf9be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot\\cos{\\frac{x}{2}}=\\cos{\\frac{3x}{2}}\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" /> We wish to find all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that there is at least one more solution to this equation distinct from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c0a0bc6cbf65c1a64b7c907716f335ed011177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"37\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01adb5172afbd0de886d647cc9b76c6efa91603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\cos{\\frac{x}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"34\" />, and noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69f8b29010d2f528d42ea916f22571854cecf2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\frac{3x}{2}}=4y^3-3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"38\" />, we can rearrange our equation to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/50454ab236bccee705b509e92e45a68c8dca2165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y^3=y(3+a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"21\" /> The smallest value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, which is not in our domain so we divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0125b0585cc06668085b2a70ec65a3ca7fc75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y^2=a+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />. By the trivial inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/756a604aaf08c6d481f2eeda2bea66891068f5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3\\ge{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afd84fc1e7b2b81858563631a3348cc7bba8ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\neq{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1ffd1cbd4c86c6bf2393821c720c80b0c8558048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+3&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. Also, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa5b61af3eb613f029161d897e1a7bc1e301ebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-2$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, then the solution to this equation would be shared with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c0a0bc6cbf65c1a64b7c907716f335ed011177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"37\" />, so there would only be one distinct solution. Finally, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b5ccd436d776b90a1db791d3bb0385da3788cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\le{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> due to the restrictions of a sine wave, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a70d77c0aead032f14411a8299629f7617f660a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\neq{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> due to the restrictions on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46bb693c803a9d34a8776528416ccf61f861408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3&lt;a&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/2328c544dc1de84530a5c172cac796c9cb549355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq{-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bc147ceb82295aedfdd7cbf1e2d72a78d27b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=-3,q=-2, r=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"17\" />, so our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec52603a9da72c2338614c90c60664c7a5dbaca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3+(-2)+1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } {-}4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"210\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~sigma\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution 1 (Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Tl5hBEkHzbA\">https://youtu.be/Tl5hBEkHzbA</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0gCMvUmZtpI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0gCMvUmZtpI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A\">2022 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2022 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017132905\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.071 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 581/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17455/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.827      1 -total\n 54.80%    7.577      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 43.65%    6.036      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23296:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017132905 and revision id 254127. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}